# The Bolt prefill head on the 3090: the attention term of a prompt is the plain prefill
# launches of the split entry (any group of a multiple of eight query heads a key head).
kind: baseline
question: does the head keep its derived prefill-attention term on the 3090, and where do its P=512/4096 rows land beside llama.cpp?
term: pp tok/s @ P = 512 (the row's pp_tok/s), ours = generate_qwen3moe built at the head under test, RTX 3090
unit: tok/s
predict: 540..600
condition: one lease on the 3090 (BLOOMERY_TIMING_GPU = the 3090), BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=2; arms 512 4096 lcpppp:512
  lcpppp:4096
reason: the room-gated G1's measured 495.62 tok/s at P=512 ran the per-row segment path:
  16,384 launches x 8.08 us = 0.132 s of a 1.033 s pass; the split entry serves a pass-layer in
  48 enqueues (~0.4 ms), so t ~0.901 s. The band widens for the rest of the head's own delta.
decide-in: the head's pp line stands; the gap to llama.cpp prices the next lever
decide-below: the launch term did not come back: nsys the pass at the head
decide-above: the segment term was overstated, or the head moved more than this term
